ProbDesc:
17-20ML-04 & 17-20ML-70 STEP 4.2.2; 
“Sight through the TI telescope and, if necessary, rotate the target collimator about its optical axis so that the telescope and collimator horizontal reticle lines are parallel. Then adjust the TI azimuth and elevation screws to position the point in the target collimator field where the horizontal and vertical reticle lines intersect near the top of the TI vertical reticle lines.”

17-20ML-12 STEP 4.1.5.2;
Perform the necessary operations to center the TI reticle on the collimator infinity target so that the TI and collimator reticle lines are parallel; e.g., tilt the TI or the collimator, move the TI or collimator from side to side, slightly rotate the TI or collimator about its optical axis (the TI reticle lines should be approximately vertical and horizontal), etc.

I am asking for a way to rotate the 272-15 in the tube of the 270BN while sighting through the TI for auto collimation vertically and horizontally.

Request Addition of model 6000FS1 “Positector” Thickness Gage to CPAR. This specific configuration is Not listed in METPRO or CPAR, however many other DeFelsko 6000 series Positector probe/body configurations are already listed.  Subject 6000FS1 is the same as model 6000F1 already listed in METPRO, but instead of a built-in sensor, its sensor is attached via a cable.    Amplifying Info: 6000 is the general instrument series; the final 1 or 3 denotes either a standard or advanced version body/display; and 1-3 letters denote the type of probe module attached to the body/display. These three elements combine to create a specific DeFelsko Positector part number.

